A||||9||85ZainoGT||Can we fit 6x9's in the 4x10 dash spots?||||4||
Z||000000||85ZainoGT||09-15-2001||01:39 AM||||is that possible? what needs to be done?||||reg||4
Z||000001||Spiff||09-15-2001||01:52 AM||||I dont think its possible. You would have to cut the dash opennings. Why not get a set of 4 inch component speakers and put them in there. I am planning on doing just that in the near future.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||SLYGUY||09-15-2001||03:23 AM||||I don't think it's possible. I just made a few mods on the stereo in my 88GT and asked about putting 6x9s in there. You can, but it has to be a surface mount. Then they would rest above the dash and look a little stupid. I belive there are a few manufacturers that still make the 4x10. One of them is Kenwood. I'm gonna stick with that. I added a Kenwood deck with 6 disck CD changer and am very happy with it. <P>Turns out that the left front 4x10 wasn't blown after all. The stock radio just made it sound that way. The rears were silent. After the new radio they weren't. I wanted to stay stock, but people in cars in the lanes next to me might of been wondering why I was singing to myself!!! LOL<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||SLYGUY||09-15-2001||03:30 AM||||Anybody have a clue as to where someone would put bass speakers? I can't imagine where you would fit any. <BR>I was considering 10-12" speakers, but can't figure out where. The amp will have to go on the bulkhead behind one of the seats. Is this gonna be dangerous? What is back there before I drill?<P>Sly<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/SLYGUYSIG.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||09-15-2001||08:19 AM||||I've got 6x9s in my Formula. They aren't surface mounted. I used stock speaker grills, no dash cutting. I installed them under the dash with some home-made templates. They sound better than any 4x10 I've heard to date.<BR>I bought a pair of Boston Acoustics and installed them, but most any brand should work. I had to remove the dash to it, but that isn't difficult to do.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Banzai||09-15-2001||10:06 AM||||for some bass you can build a triangular box to fit the front of the passenger side footwell---- with about .5 to .7 cu. ft. innner volume. get a 10" Kicker Solobaric and run at least 100 QUALITY watts to it (no cheap amps) you will be impressed.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||Sootah||09-15-2001||03:11 PM||||My friend has the 5.25" Kappa Infinity component set in the dash. You want quality, get those. Nothing compares.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif">   <BR><I>Never pull your pants down in Cosco, the dang monkeys will getcha</I> <BR><B>AIM</B>: KSSouter||||reg||1
Z||000007||Alex4mula||09-15-2001||11:03 PM||||Here in FL they sell a plastic adapter to install 6x9 in a 4x10 hole. The problem is that it lowers the speaker about an inch and I don't think there's enough space down there in the drivers side for that. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||recluse||09-15-2001||11:23 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SLYGUY:<BR><B>Anybody have a clue as to where someone would put bass speakers? I can't imagine where you would fit any. <BR>I was considering 10-12" speakers, but can't figure out where. The amp will have to go on the bulkhead behind one of the seats. Is this gonna be dangerous? What is back there before I drill?<P>Sly<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>As far as bass speakers go...  I had two 10's in small boxes, one behind each seat, but you have to move the seats all the way up.  I also had my amp mounted behind the drivers seat on the firewall.  Above the carpet on the fiber board or whatever that material is.  Just run some short drywall type screws in, you dont even need to drill any holes... worked good for me.<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Spektrum-87GT||09-16-2001||12:42 AM||||i'm starting on my installation of two 12s and two 6x9s tomorrow. i'll take pics of the finished install when i'm done. If you want an idea of what I'm going to do... basically going to mount 2 long boxes, dimensions looking aft(er, standing at the front of the car, looking to the back) width: 15" height: 30" length: 7". basically its going to be split up into 2 divisions. the top near the headrest is going to house the 6x9s and the bottom is going to store the 12s. I know some of you crazy competition sound fanatics are probably cringing, but hey, its great for cruising around. And to the comment about cheap amps... there's nothing wrong with my cheap profile amp! 300x2(no really, it is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">) amp driving 2 generic subs, i like my amp more than my friends 200x2 rockford fosgate and there is *minimal* quality difference to the NORMAL human ear. Mine also can out-bass his and costed a quarter of the price.||||reg||1
